## Lore

Wampyrs (pronounced vom-peers) are a strange breed of vampire. Like true
vampires they were hunted and converted by the slow kill, but something in these
victims was different. Some occultists speculate they were true innocents or pure
souls; others that some people are simply too strong-willed for the vampiric
domination to take hold; and a third theory holds that Wampyrs were latent
Nightbane whose supernatural origins made them partially immune. Nobody,
including the vampire intelligences, knows the truth.

They are still inhuman: they need blood, and light hurts them and will kill them
over time. But unlike true vampires they are free to choose the path of their
lives. Many try to lead a normal life and hide their natures from family and
loved ones; others become criminals and predators as dangerous as any vampire.
Several have declared war on their blood-sucking cousins - the mysterious Iosef
Pendragon, founder of the Nocturnes, is one - and some have allied themselves
with Nightbane, human sorcerers and even rebellious secondary vampires.

A Wampyr can be killed by guns and knives, and below zero it is as close to death
as any human, and it cannot become mist, bat or wolf. In exchange, sunlight harms
it far more slowly, and running water, holy symbols, herbs and native soil mean
nothing to it. Vampire intelligences and master vampires hate and fear Wampyrs as
aberrations and a danger to the whole undead species, and attack them on sight
without giving or asking quarter.

## GM Notes

**Alliances and allies.** Wampyrs often work with human vampire hunters and
other enemies of the vampires. Some become minions of the Nightlords just for
the chance to destroy them or their undead cousins - the Nightlords use Wampyrs
to hunt true vampires - but only evil or anarchist characters would consider it.
Good and anarchist Wampyrs are frequently, if warily, accepted into groups of
humans and Nightbane. Guardians find them disturbing and avoid direct contact,
but do not destroy them on sight as they do true vampires, and some have let a
good Wampyr join their group.

**Alignment.** Scrupulous Wampyrs avoid drinking the blood of unwilling people.

**Average life span.** Unknown, possibly limitless.

**Money.** Typically 2D4x100 dollars in cash and 2D6x1,000 dollars in property,
including vehicles and equipment.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-wampyr');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-wampyr';

